<section class="section-light" aria-labelledby="types-heading">
  <div class="container">
    <div class="fade-up" style="max-width:680px;">
      <span class="eyebrow">Types of Grafts</span>
      <h2 id="types-heading" class="section-heading">Matched to Your Anatomy</h2>
      <span class="gold-rule"></span>
    </div>
    <div class="card-grid" style="margin-top:var(--space-lg);">
      <div class="card fade-up">
        <h3>Socket Preservation</h3>
        <p>Placed at the time of tooth extraction, this graft preserves the socket walls so that bone loss is minimized from the start.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="card fade-up">
        <h3>Ridge Augmentation</h3>
        <p>When existing bone has already shrunk, ridge augmentation rebuilds volume along the jaw ridge to accommodate implants.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="card fade-up">
        <h3>Sinus Lift</h3>
        <p>For upper-jaw implants when the sinus cavity sits too close to the jaw crest, a sinus lift elevates the sinus floor and places graft material beneath it.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
    <p class="fade-up" style="margin-top:var(--space-lg);color:var(--mid-gray);">For patients with extreme upper-jaw bone loss who cannot undergo sinus lift, <a href="/zygomatic-implants" style="color:var(--navy);font-weight:600;">zygomatic implants</a> may offer a path that avoids grafting altogether.</p>
  </div>
</section>

